# Every text file checks out with LF, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference — it is a correctness requirement. The exporter
# embeds its inputs byte-for-byte: theme SVGs and images become base64 `data:`
# URIs, theme CSS is inlined into the document, and `pipeline.test.ts` compares
# the result against a committed golden file whose `<style>` bodies and data URIs
# are recorded as byte counts. A CRLF checkout changes those bytes, so the same
# commit produces a different document on Windows than on macOS or Linux — which
# is exactly what the first Windows CI run reported, as a logo whose base64 was
# 12 bytes longer.
#
# Nothing in this repository needs CRLF: there are no .bat, .cmd or .ps1 files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary — never inspected or converted.
*.webp binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.vsix binary

# Byte-exact fixtures and rendered artifacts: belt and braces on top of the
# repo-wide rule above.
test-fixtures/**       -text
themes/**/sample*.html -text
